---
/* The question that opens a case study, optically aligned to the column.

   The box edges already line up: the lede and the paragraph under it both
   start at the same x. What does not line up is the INK, because the display
   italic and the body face carry different left side bearings, and in
   Instrument Serif italic the bearing changes sign from letter to letter. An
   H or a D hangs about 0.036em LEFT of its origin, while a W sits 0.088em to
   the RIGHT of it. So there is no single nudge that fixes this: shifting
   everything right by one value squares up SaveEat and pushes the tooth page
   visibly too far in.

   The table is the measured bearing of each capital, taken from the rendered
   font with TextMetrics.actualBoundingBoxLeft at 44px and divided by the font
   size, so it holds at any lede size. Positive means ink sits left of the
   origin and the line has to move right by that much.

   The constant is the body face doing the same thing: its capitals average
   1.13px of ink to the RIGHT of their origin at 18px, so the lede is lined up
   to where the paragraph's ink actually starts rather than to its box.

   Re-measure both if --font-display or --font-text ever changes.
*/
const BEARING_EM = {
  A: 0.074, B: 0.036, C: -0.055, D: 0.036, E: 0.036, F: 0.036, G: -0.052,
  H: 0.036, I: 0.036, J: 0.152, K: 0.036, L: 0.036, M: 0.043, N: 0.042,
  O: -0.054, P: 0.036, Q: 0.032, R: 0.036, S: -0.003, T: -0.051, U: -0.064,
  V: -0.088, W: -0.088, X: 0.036, Y: -0.057, Z: 0.04,
};
const BODY_INK_PX = 1.13;

const { text } = Astro.props;
const first = String(text ?? '').trim().charAt(0).toUpperCase();
const bearing = BEARING_EM[first];
/* An unlisted opener (a digit, a quote mark) gets no correction rather than a
   guessed one: no shift is a smaller error than the wrong shift. */
const indent = bearing === undefined ? undefined : `text-indent:calc(${bearing}em + ${BODY_INK_PX}px)`;
---
<p class="lede" style={indent}>{text}</p>
